          "hpc": 6,
          "semantic": 3
        },
        "by": "human",
        "reason": "Downstream SQL-on-FHIR consumers join derived tables on getResourceKey() resource keys, which the port computes internally but drops at the outermost SELECT. The attempt adds the paired key column beside each MIMIC identifier column (subject_id->patient_key, hadm_id->encounter_key, stay_id->icu_encounter_key, specimen_id->specimen_key). Additive and shape-only: both comparison paths project manifest columns explicitly, so no compared value can change. The MIMIC integer columns are retained as the oracle join keys.",
        "superseded_decided_by": "judge",
        "superseded_error": null,
        "superseded_justification": "Judge accepted attempt_0006: mimic-fhir/sql/fhir_observation_chartevents.sql:9,67 irreversibly normalizes spring-forward chartevents charttime before writing Observation.effectiveDateTime. The comparator found 287078/287152 identical rows, with 16 key-shift pairs and 32 residual collision losses producing 26 conflicts; the original wall time is unrecoverable by permissible FHIR queries because it survives only in opaque Observation.id identity. All defensible mappings were exhausted and this is the contract's accepted New York DST transformation loss.",
